{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Cap Nursing Student Places in alignment with planned Newly Qualified Nurse jobs",
        "additional_details": "Nursing students spend 3 years completing demanding degrees and clinical placements, contributing to patient care. Many graduates find limited vacancies, recruitment freezes, no suitable jobs, and significant student loan debt.\r\n\r\nWe call for:\r\nTransparency: Publish graduate employment prospects, local vacancies and recruitment forecasts.\r\nAnnual reporting: Disclose expected Band 5 vacancies, recruitment targets and student placement numbers.\r\nCap admissions responsibly: Cap university places at a level that's aligned with assessed workforce needs and vacancies.\r\nFair employment: Review and fund more coordinated pathways into nursing for newly qualified graduates.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to cap the number of nursing students based on actual planned NHS vacancies, and publish statistics on Band 5 vacancies for newly qualified nurses to help ensure students are informed of realistic employment prospects before committing to a degree and student loan debt.",
